From: XXRI OS Team
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the keyboard focus when the last window closes

throw_focus() hands the focus to another frame; with no frame left it did
nothing, and the X server then reverted the focus to None - all keyboard
input discarded, no hotkey (Alt+Esc, Ctrl+Alt+C, the Super key that opens
All Apps) reachable until a window was opened with the mouse.  Fall back to
PointerRoot.
---
--- a/Frame.C
+++ b/Frame.C
@@ -977,6 +977,12 @@
   if (revert_to && revert_to->activate()) return;
   for (Frame* f = first; f; f = f->next)
     if (f != this && f->activate()) return;
+#ifdef XXRI
+  // Nobody took it. GTK windows set RevertToParent, so the server would
+  // revert to None and drop all keyboard input, hotkeys included. Give an
+  // empty desktop PointerRoot instead.
+  XSetInputFocus(fl_display, PointerRoot, RevertToPointerRoot, CurrentTime);
+#endif
 }
 
